.TH "BASH\-SERVER\-DEBUG" "7" "2026\-02\-01" "bash\-server 0.1.0" "bash\-server concepts"
.SH DESCRIPTION
bash\-server includes an interactive debugger that operates over
CHAN_DEBUG (channel 4) in the v2 protocol.
The debugger allows clients to set breakpoints, control execution flow,
and inspect the abstract syntax tree (AST) of pending commands.
All debugger interaction occurs within a single forked session process,
so pausing execution is safe and does not block the server or other
sessions.
.SH CONCEPTS
.SH Breakpoint types
Three breakpoint types are supported, each matching commands in a
different way:
.PP
\f[B]Command breakpoints\f[R] (\f[CR]DBG_BREAK_COMMAND\f[R]): Match
against the command string using pattern matching.
The pattern is compared to the textual representation of each command
before execution.
.PP
\f[B]Line breakpoints\f[R] (\f[CR]DBG_BREAK_LINE\f[R]): Match against
the source line number.
Useful when evaluating scripts or multi\-line command strings where the
line number is meaningful.
.PP
\f[B]Function breakpoints\f[R] (\f[CR]DBG_BREAK_FUNC\f[R]): Match
against the function name when a shell function is invoked.
